<div class="exercise"><div class="ex-q"><p>A 1 kHz reference is multiplied by a 1.05 kHz signal. Which frequencies appear in the product?</p>
</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class="ex-s"><p>50 Hz (the difference) and 2.05 kHz (the sum). A low-pass filter at, say, 200 Hz keeps only the 50 Hz beat: this is heterodyning, used in radios and in some encoder interpolators.</p>
</div></details></div>
